From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:51:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/layer-shell: Destroy the layer surface resource with
 its role

If the client destroys the wl_surface first, the role object is
finalized while the zwlr_layer_surface_v1 resource is still alive, and
requests on it would reach freed memory. Destroy the resource with the
role, as xdg_toplevel does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-layer-shell.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-layer-shell.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-layer-shell.c
index b150ba2..6bd94f5 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-layer-shell.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-layer-shell.c
@@ -1096,10 +1096,11 @@ meta_wayland_layer_surface_finalize (GObject *object)
 {
   MetaWaylandLayerSurface *layer_surface = META_WAYLAND_LAYER_SURFACE (object);
 
+  /* As for xdg_toplevel, the role object goes with the wl_surface. */
   if (layer_surface->resource)
     {
-      wl_resource_set_user_data (layer_surface->resource, NULL);
       wl_resource_set_destructor (layer_surface->resource, NULL);
+      g_clear_pointer (&layer_surface->resource, wl_resource_destroy);
     }
 
   if (layer_surface->layer_shell)
